=TITLE Raku: The History

=SUBTITLE Learn about the History of Raku

=head1 The Readable History

The readable version of the history is contained in the following three articles:

=begin table
Decade                   | Years     | Summary
========================
L<The First Decade|http://strangelyconsistent.org/blog/happy-10th-anniversary-perl-6> | 2000-2010 | Design and Beginnings |
------------------------
L<The Second Decade|???> (not yet written) | 2010-2020 | Building and Renaming |
------------------------
L<The Third Decade|???> (not yet written) | 2020-2025 | AST and Ecosystem |
=end table

=head1 Timeline

Please add other events to this timeline

=begin table
Date       | Event
==================
2000-07-18 | The Jon Orwant Mug Throwing Incident, at the Perl Conference 4.0 (July 17-20, 2000)
------------------
2000       | L<Larry's Speech|https://web.archive.org/web/20221206183705/https://raku.org/archive/talks/2000/als/larry-als.txt>
------------------
2005-02-02 | A. Tang L<announces|https://www.mail-archive.com/perl6-all@perl.org/msg45008.html> beginning implementation of Pugs
------------------
2005       | Patrick Michaud begins implemeting what would (in 2008) become Rakudo on Parrot
------------------
2009-03-17 | Parrot 1.0 released
------------------
2010-07-29 | Rakudo Star released
------------------
2017-10-02 | Final commit to Parrot
------------------
2021-08    | Parrot discontinued (replaced with MoarVM)
------------------
=end table

